          {
            title: 'Cangkul',
            subtitle: 'Indonesian Shedding',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Cangkul is a popular Indonesian card game where players try to get rid of all their cards by following suit. The name 'Cangkul' means 'to dig with a hoe' in Indonesian, referring to digging through the stock pile for playable cards. Similar games include Burro (Spain) and Donkey (Goa).",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Indonesia. Cangkul ('to dig with a hoe'): shedding game; 3â€“5p, 52 cards, 7 each. Follow suit; can't follow = draw from stock until playable; stock empty = pass and pick up trick. Similar to Burro in Spain and Donkey in Goa.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3â€“5. Each for themselves.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards (A high). Optional joker as wild in some variants.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52-card deck; optional joker.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '7 cards each; remainder is face-down stock. Clockwise.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
